WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
01 / A FINISHED NEWSLETTER
The current design engine turns the brief into a photo-led, branded asset.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
02 / GIVE THE AGENT A BRIEF
Group, dates, transport, and activities. One saved conversation.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.000
03 / OPEN THE SAVED DRAFT
The finished asset stays linked to the request, waiting for review.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.000
04 / READ THE TRIP DETAILS
Structured content becomes a consistent layout, with dates and a next step.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.000
ALSO / A DAY-BY-DAY ITINERARY
The current canvas renderer produces a clear schedule for the group leader.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.000
ALSO / A TWO-SIDED HANDOUT
The same workflow supports a photo-led handout with trip details and a next step.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.000
05 / ASK FOR A REVISION
Warmer wording. More free time. The work stays in the same conversation.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.000
06 / REVIEW BEFORE APPROVING
Draft versions, further changes, and approval live beside the actual asset.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.000
07 / RECORD AN APPROVAL
Sample approval is recorded. This isolated environment sends nothing.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.000
OR / HOLD IT FOR MORE WORK
The sample draft stays available for changes, without delivery.

